    {
      "SurveyID": "SV_0Sy4z7UTkBM0ptI",
      "Element": "SQ",
      "PrimaryAttribute": "QID19",
      "SecondaryAttribute": "You must click the Next [--- ] button on this page to receive your unique completion code to get...",
      "TertiaryAttribute": null,
      "Payload": {
        "QuestionText": "<strong><span style=\"color:#e74c3c;\"><span style=\"font-size:19px;\">You must click the Next [---&gt;] button on this page to receive your unique completion code to get credit.<br>\nDo NOT close your browser yet.&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><br>\n<br>\nStudy Title:<\/strong>&nbsp;Perceptions of Communicated Information<br>\n<strong>Faculty Supervisor:<\/strong>&nbsp;Jonathan Fugelsang, PhD, Department of Psychology, University of Waterloo<br>\n<strong>Phone:<\/strong>&nbsp;+1-XXX-XXX-XXXX&nbsp;x47197, Email: researcher@example.edu<br>\n<strong>Student Investigator:<\/strong> Caroline Simpson, Department of Psychology, University of Waterloo. Email: researcher@example.edu<br>\n<br>\n<span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:200%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:200%\">Dear participant,<\/span><\/span><br>\n<br>\n<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:200%\">We appreciate your participation in our study and thank you for spending the time helping us with our research.&nbsp; The purpose of this post-study information page is to provide additional details about the study you just participated in.<\/span><\/span><br>\n<br>\n<b><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:200%\">About Today\u2019s Study:<\/span><\/span><\/b><br>\n<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:200%\">You were originally told that this study was designed to investigate what impacts perceptions of information communicated through written content.&nbsp; While we were indeed interested in studying perceptions of communication, the study objectives were more involved from what we originally explained to you.<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><\/span><br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:115%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif\">In this study, we are interested in how anthropomorphism \u2013 the attribution of human-like qualities \u2013 of a generative artificial intelligence source affects the level of trust in the content they generate.&nbsp; In other words, we wanted to see if changing the description and image of the author of a fictional blog post would change how trustworthy the author and content were perceived to be. This study is important because of the recent prevalence of generative AI sources and content, combined with past research has suggested that when machines are anthropomorphized, they are perceived as more trustworthy.&nbsp;Examining factors that potentially influence perception of trustworthiness can add to our theoretical understanding of cognition. Additionally, this work can inform appropriate use of anthropomorphism techniques in the technology and media industries.<br>\n<br>\nParticipants in this study were randomized into one of 3 conditions. They either read a description of an author that was a human expert (high anthropomorphism), an intentionally anthropomorphized generative AI agent (medium anthropomorphism), or a non-anthropomorphized generative AI agent (low anthropomorphism). You were in the&nbsp;<\/span><\/span><\/span>${e:\/\/Field\/Condition}<span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:115%\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Aptos&quot;,sans-serif\"> anthropomorphism condition.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\nThe reason we needed to use partial disclosure in this study was because we needed participants\u2019 behaviour and attitudes to be as natural as possible. We apologize again for not providing you with complete and accurate information about the purpose and objectives for this study, but we hope you understand why this was necessary. If you have questions about the use of partial disclosure in this study, please contact one of the researchers listed by email.<br>\n<br>\nSince this study involves some aspects that you were not told about before starting, it is very important that you not discuss your experiences with any other people who potentially could be in this study, until the completion of the study.&nbsp; If people come into the study knowing about our specific predictions, as you can imagine, it could influence their results, and the data we collect would not be usable.&nbsp; Also, if you print off a copy of this post-study information page, please do not make it available to others.<br>\n<br>\n<b>Confidentiality:<\/b><br>\nYour identity will be confidential. Furthermore, because the interest of this study is in the average responses of the entire group of participants, you will not be identified individually in any way in any written reports of this research. The data, with identifying information removed, will be kept for a period of at least 7 years following publication of the research, after which it will be deleted. The data will be securely stored to which only researchers associated with this study have access.<br>\n<br>\nDe-identified data related to your participation may be submitted to an online repository and \/ or journal (i.e., the data may be publicly available). These data will be completely deidentified\/anonymized prior to submission and will be presented in aggregate form in publications. This process is integral to the research process as it allows other researchers to verify results and avoid duplicating research. Though the data is posted for the purpose listed, other individuals may access these data by accessing the open access repository. Although the dataset without identifiers may be shared publicly, your identity will always remain confidential.<br>\n<br>\n<b>Data Storage:<\/b><br>\nThe research data will be securely stored on secure University of Waterloo Servers or as needed, on encrypted external drives, for a minimum of seven years, and will be accessible to members of the research team only. You may decide to withdraw from this study at any time by closing this webpage and may do so without loss of remuneration. Once data has been collected, you may request your data be removed from the study up until 30 days from the day of your participation by contacting one of the researchers listed above with your unique completion code.<br>\n&nbsp;<br>\n<b>Ethics clearance:<\/b><br>\nThis study has been reviewed and received ethics clearance through a University of Waterloo Research Ethics Board (REB [#XXXXX]). If you have questions for the Board, contact the Office of Research Ethics, toll-free at +1-XXX-XXX-XXXX (Canada and USA), +1-XXX-XXX-XXXX, or researcher@example.edu. For all other questions contact one of the researchers named above.<br>\n<br>\n<b>Questions:<\/b><br>\nIf you are interested in receiving more information regarding the results of this study, or would like a summary of the results, please reach out to the investigator indicating your interest, and when the study is completed, we will send you the information. In the meantime, if you have any questions about the study, please do not hesitate to contact the investigator by email.<br>\n<br>\nThank you again for your participation. Without the help of participants like you, important research in psychology would not be possible.<\/span><\/span><\/span><br>\n&nbsp;",
        "QuestionJS": "Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function()\n{\n\t\/*Place your JavaScript here to run when the page loads*\/\n\n});\n\nQualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnReady(function()\n{\n\t\/*Place your JavaScript here to run when the page is fully displayed*\/\n\tlet length = 12;\n\tlet result = '';\n    const characters = 'ABCDEFGHJKLMNPQRSTUVWXYZ23456789';\n    const charactersLength = characters.length;\n    let counter = 0;\n    while (counter < length) {\n        result += characters.charAt(Math.floor(Math.random() * charactersLength));\n        counter += 1;\n    }\n\t\n\tQualtrics.SurveyEngine.setEmbeddedData('completion_code', result);\n    });\n\nQualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnUnload(function()\n{\n\t\/*Place your JavaScript here to run when the page is unloaded*\/\n\n\n});",
        "DefaultChoices": false,
